    {
      "id": "sol.hmmt-nov-guts-2013-p23.hmmt",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "\\(\\quad(991,997,1009)\\) Let \\(f(x)=x(x-12)(x+6)+320=x^{3}-6 x^{2}-72 x+320\\), so that \\(f(1001)=989 \\cdot 1001 \\cdot 1007+320\\). But \\(f(4)=4(-8)(10)+320=0\\), so \\(f(x)=(x-4)\\left(x^{2}-2 x-80\\right)=\\) \\((x-4)(x-10)(x+8)\\).\nThus \\(f(1001)=991 \\cdot 997 \\cdot 1009\\), as desired.",
